alogy, with no direct test in a relevant system.","criteria":"Use when sources describe a mechanism or a claimed idea but show no tested result for this use. A patent without test data is Theoretical.","examples":["A technique proven in pharmaceutical tablets that has never been tested in a food matrix."],"strength":1,"rules":{"allow_no_sources":false,"any_of":[{"min_sources":1}]}},{"key":"our_hypothesis","name":"Our hypothesis","definition":"An inference made by this system, not stated by any retrieved source.","criteria":"Use for any connection, transfer or prediction you reasoned yourself. The rationale must say what it is based on and how it could be tested.","examples":["Applying a barrier approach used in medical packaging to a snack pack may extend shelf life; no source tests this."],"strength":0,"rules":{"allow_no_sources":true}}]}$ph$::jsonb, 'active', '[]'::jsonb, $ph$v2 adds strength and rules. Established science above Experimental above Theoretical above Our hypothesis. Demonstrated commercial use is a separate dimension and has no strength. Only paper, review, technical report and standard sources count toward Established science.$ph$, now());

insert into public.evidence_labels (prompt_version_id, key, name, definition, criteria)
select pv.id, v.key, v.name, v.definition, v.criteria
from public.prompt_versions pv, jsonb_to_recordset(pv.parsed->'labels') as v(key text, name text, definition text, criteria text)
where pv.kind = 'evidence_labels' and pv.status = 'active';

